          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Meesho Says 70% of Its Code Is Now AI-Written as Revenue Jumps 47% to Rs 3,531 Crore in Q4",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "Indian e-commerce platform Meesho has disclosed that over 70% of its codebase is now generated using artificial intelligence, with more than three-quarters of its orders driven by an AI recommendation engine. The company posted a 47% revenue jump to Rs 3,531 crore in Q4 FY26, narrowing its net loss by 88% year-on-year to Rs 166 crore. CEO Vidit Aatrey framed AI not just as a productivity tool but as a core commercial engine powering Meesho's path to profitability.",
            "url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/technology/meesho-q4-revenue-jumps-47-operating-losses-widen-on-aggressive-growth-push/articleshow/130860891.cms",
